<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE logger SYSTEM "logger.dtd">
<!--
  SUBUWUTUNER FA-DIT LOGGER SUPPLEMENT — VERSION 0001

  Purpose
  =======
  RomRaider's public logger XML (v370, last released Nov 2021) does not
  include `<ecuparam>` entries for any FA-DIT VA / VB WRX ecuid we have
  encountered, including the ones documented in
  fixtures/private/PAK_DECODE_RESULTS.md (A629B07507 = LF75600H,
  D829B07107 = LF9L000E, plus 23 others). The OEM-side commercial tools
  cover these ECUs but their data is not redistributable.

  This file is the SubuwuTuner-native extension point: a small, additive
  logger XML that follows the RomRaider DTD so `tools/defgen/loggergen.py`
  can consume it alongside v370. Hardware-captured RAM addresses for
  extended parameters land here, with provenance attached per entry.

  Workflow for adding a new entry
  ================================
  1. Capture: connect a verified J2534 adapter to the running ECU and
     run `subuwutuner-cli rom-pull ...` to dump the ROM. The dump's
     ecuid (printed by `rom-info`) is the value that goes into the
     <ecu id="..."> attribute.
  2. Discover: identify the live-RAM address for the parameter of
     interest. Two paths:
     a) Side-by-side with an equivalent OEM logger session (legal in
        most contexts as long as no commercial tool's IP is copied
        into this file) — note the requested address.
     b) RAM-watching via a custom feature graph in `st::feature::ir`
        that exfiltrates a watch list; this is the path that does not
        depend on any third-party tool.
  3. Document: add the <ecuparam> entry below with `provenance` set
     to "hardware" / "side-by-side" / "ram-watch" plus your contact.
     Never paste an address pulled from a commercial-tool decompile
     into this file. See `docs/15-clean-room-engineering.md` for the
     full rules.

  Loggergen integration
  =====================
  loggergen.py currently takes one XML at a time. To process the
  supplement alongside v370, run loggergen twice and union the
  resulting ecuparams (the loader in `st::defs` handles ecuparam
  fragments cumulatively). A `merge` flag is on the v1.x roadmap.

  Status
  ======
  This file is intentionally near-empty in its initial commit. The
  shell + a single STUB entry is included to (a) prove the DTD
  parses, (b) round-trip through loggergen, and (c) give contributors
  a template. The STUB entry MUST be removed once a real entry lands
  with verified address + provenance; do not ship the stub.
-->
<logger>
    <protocols>
        <protocol id="SSM" baud="4800" databits="8" stopbits="1" parity="0" connect_timeout="2000" send_timeout="55">
            <ecuparams>

                <!--
                  STUB — replace with real entries.
                  Demonstrates the structure loggergen expects. Address
                  0xFFFFFF is a sentinel that defs-loader can reject.
                -->
                <ecuparam id="X1" name="STUB - Replace Me" desc="Placeholder to keep loggergen happy until a real ecuparam lands. Address is a sentinel.">
                    <ecu id="A629B07507,D829B07107">
                        <address length="1">0xFFFFFF</address>
                    </ecu>
                    <conversions>
                        <conversion units="raw" expr="x" format="0" />
                    </conversions>
                </ecuparam>

                <!--
                  FUTURE ENTRIES go here, one <ecuparam> per logical
                  signal. Group by signal (fuel, knock, boost, etc.)
                  and within each group keep entries alphabetically by
                  ecuid for easy diff review.

                  Suggested initial discovery priorities (per the
                  under-served-coverage thesis in docs/05 §11):

                    1. Per-cylinder fine knock learn (FLKC) — feeds
                       the per-cylinder knock dashboard.
                    2. DAM (Dynamic Advance Multiplier) — drives the
                       adaptive-learning history visualizer.
                    3. EBCS / WGDC PID gains (live) — for the
                       boost-controller PID assistant.
                    4. ECT-conditioned cold-start state — for the
                       cold-start tuning workflow.
                -->

            </ecuparams>
        </protocol>
    </protocols>
</logger>
